{"reference":"2 Chronicles 34","book":"2 Chronicles","chapter":34,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"How the chapter holds together","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The chapter presents Josiah’s reforms as a connected sequence: after the temple is repaired, a book of the law is found and read publicly; Huldah delivers an oracle; and Josiah leads the people in renewing their covenant before removing further abominations. This sequence frames the reforms as extending from the discovered book and the response it prompts.","verse_refs":["2 Chronicles 34:1-33"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_2_chronicles_034_0a5e06baa51bd1b4bf94adfc"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}